{
  "version": 1,
  "updated": "2026-11-27",
  "about": "The meta-backend lane's backend -> stand-in map (meta/backend.mjs). One entry per backend a server's write tools can write to that may run inside a GitHub Actions job: the engine itself, or a self-hostable product, or an open-source stand-in for a hosted API. `signals` say how the lane recognises it in a repository (meta/README.md, \"meta-backend\"); `stand_in` says what writecheck's full mode would run. A subject is local_full only when its primary backend's stand-in has fidelity real or faithful AND cleared true. fidelity: real = the product itself; faithful = another implementation of the same API whose own semantics (versions, conflicts, transactions) hold; partial = the same API without the semantics writecheck's backend requirements need; not_faithful = a different API (a look-alike). cleared: the stand-in's licence and terms allow the loop to run it with no account, token or paid licence (false = a person has to decide). Sources: company-audit research/writecheck-coverage-2026-11-28/RESEARCH.md, section 2, and each product's own licence. Add a backend or change a stand-in here, not in code; meta/test/backend.test.mjs checks the shape. A backend that is also a hosted API with a published description has an entry of the same id in spec-urls.json; both are merged.",
